license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For the star K_{1,a} with one edge subdivided, B_a, and all a, r >= 3 and n >= (r-1)a+1, the r-uniform Berge saturation number is floor(a(n+1)/((r-1)a+1)), attained by disjoint loose stars; saturated hypergraphs near the minimum are loose stars up to a bounded remainder. For a >= 5, B_a is the unique tree on a+2 vertices with the least asymptotic lower three-uniform Berge saturation coefficient, the Berge analogue of a theorem of Faudree, Faudree, Gould and Jacobson. A Lean proof of the exact formula and the structure theorem is included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
keywords:
